            ("Clingman and Monroe", "James Monroe, Frederick Muhlenberg, and Abraham Venable confronted him with accusations carried by James Reynolds and Jacob Clingman. Hamilton showed them evidence of the affair, then later blamed Monroe when the story became public."),
            ("Camillus and Jay's Treaty", "Under the name Camillus, he wrote an extended defense of Jay's Treaty against attacks from Jeffersonian Republicans. The essays linked his constitutional argument for executive treaty power to a strongly pro-British commercial policy."),
